Maintainer: Angel Robles-Fernandez <a.l.robles.fernandez@gmail.com>
Description:
  Bayesian estimation of the fundamental niche as a multivariate normal
  ellipsoid from occurrence data using Stan via cmdstanr, with phylogenetic
  evolutionary models (BM, OU) and ancestral state reconstruction. The
  package implements the presence-only likelihood of Jimenez et al.
  (2019) <doi:10.1016/j.ecolmodel.2018.11.013> with full posterior
  inference for niche centroid, tolerance (sigma) and correlation (rho).
  Evolutionary models include Brownian motion and Ornstein-Uhlenbeck
  processes on niche parameters, with optional evolution of the covariance
  structure. All models support reduce_sum parallelisation for HPC
  workflows.
